{{also|indifférence}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|indifférence|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{term|indifferentia|lang=la}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-indifference.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The state of being [[indifferent]].
# [[unbiased|Unbiased]] [[impartiality]].
# [[unemotional|Unemotional]] [[apathy]].
#* His daughter's '''indifference''' towards the sexist group made him wonder if she was even human.
# A lack of [[enthusiasm]].
# [[unconcerned|Unconcerned]] [[nonchalance]].
#* {{quote-book|year=1897|author=[[w:Winston Churchill (novelist)|Winston Churchill]]
|title=[[w:The Celebrity|The Celebrity]]
|chapter=1|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL2341853W
|passage=I liked the man for his own sake, and even had he promised to turn out a celebrity it would have had no weight with me. I look upon notoriety with the same '''indifference''' as on the buttons on a man's shirt-front, or the crest on his note-paper.}}

